(Bug #66, the flag half. Bug #32 made the ANALYZER's flag types
 order-independent; codegen's stayed ordered, so a flag read inside a
 function defined above its schema printed the address of the flag's own
 default string. No flag is supplied on the command line, so every read
 answers the declared default.)

To 'show the flags'.
    Print output.
    Print retries.
    Print verbose.

a flag called output is "-o" or "--output", it is a text with default "out.txt".
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number with default 3.
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.

'show the flags'.

Print output.
Print retries.
Print verbose.
